The full theorem remains open. I proved a uniform all-scale bound for the Gaussian one-vertex expansion, including arbitrary initial degree,
\[
\|(A_{h-1}-A_h)V\|_{\rho,s}
\le C\gamma^{2h}\|V\|_{H,s+1}.
\]
This gives summable linear marginal shifts and a continuous first-order Fermi counterterm. The off-half-filled UV initialization and first infrared integration are also established using the existing finite-integration results.

The missing step is the nonlinear renormalized-tree bound with uniform endpoint, history and source estimates. Lemma N states it explicitly. I proved a joint Brouwer closure conditional on those bounds, and explained how the source estimates would transfer the dimensions \(K\) and \(1/K\).

The numerical controls pass. They do not test the interacting RG.

